import ../../helpers/driver.dl

appearance image appearance:
    maximum width is 200
    padding is 10
    corner radius is 8

appearance cropped appearance:
    height is 100
    image fit is cover

document image test:
    picture "Landscape" from "landscape.webp" using image appearance
    picture "Duplicate" from "landscape.webp" using cropped appearance

set instance to an instance of image test
set view to a UI view of (the address of instance) sized 400 by 400 using font "regular" with the test UI driver
set second to a UI view of (the address of instance) sized 300 by 300 using font "regular" with the test UI driver
set surface to view's window as a pointer to test UI surface
set view's cursor to a UI point at -10.0 and -10.0
require condition (surface's image opens = 0) reporting "Image callbacks captured a temporary view during construction"
ignore update UI view the address of view
ignore update UI view the address of second
require condition (surface's image opens = 1) reporting "Repeated pictures decoded the same asset twice"
set image to UI image from "landscape.webp" in (the address of view)
require condition (image != (UI image from "landscape.webp" in (the address of second))) reporting "Two drivers shared an image resource"
require condition (image's status = 0) reporting "An asynchronous image was marked ready before decoding"
complete UI image image in (the address of view) with resource (7 as a pointer) sized 400 by 200 at status 1
ignore update UI view the address of view
require condition (view's layout's first's bounds' height = 110.0) reporting "Decoded dimensions did not determine picture height"
require condition (surface's textured > 0) reporting "The picture was not painted"
require condition ((the UI hit at (a UI point at 150.0 and 50.0) in (view's layout) during (view's paint count) for (the address of instance)) = view's layout's first) reporting "A picture did not cover hit testing behind its bounds"
set paints to surface's paints
ignore update UI view the address of view
require condition (surface's paints = paints) reporting "An idle image kept repainting"
set frame to @intrinsic("construct", UI frame, the address of view, true)
draw UI image image in (UI box at 0 0 sized 100 100) rounded by 4.0 fitting 1 on frame
set index to 0
loop while index < view's vertex count:
    set vertex to the item at index in (view's vertices)
    require condition ((0.249 <= vertex's u <= 0.751) and (0.0 <= vertex's v <= 1.0)) reporting "Cover fit stretched instead of cropping the image"
    increment index
draw UI image image in (UI box at 0 0 sized 100 100) rounded by 0.0 fitting 0 on frame
set index to 0
loop while index < view's vertex count:
    set vertex to the item at index in (view's vertices)
    require condition (24.0 <= vertex's y <= 76.0) reporting "Contain fit changed the source aspect ratio"
    increment index
set the source of picture "Landscape" in (the address of instance) to (the string form of "portrait.webp")
ignore update UI view the address of view
set portrait to UI image from "portrait.webp" in (the address of view)
complete UI image portrait in (the address of view) with resource (8 as a pointer) sized 200 by 400 at status 1
ignore update UI view the address of view
require condition (view's layout's first's bounds' height = 380.0) reporting "Changing a picture retained the previous source's aspect ratio"
set other to UI image from "broken.webp" in (the address of view)
complete UI image other in (the address of view) with resource (0 as a pointer) sized 0 by 0 at status 2
require condition (other's status = 2) reporting "An image failure was hidden"
ignore UI image from "pending.webp" in (the address of view)
release UI images in (the address of view)
require condition ((surface's image closes = 4) and (surface's image releases = 2)) reporting "Closing image resources lost a pending request or ready texture"
require condition (view's images = @intrinsic("construct", a pointer to UI image)) reporting "Released image records stayed attached to the view"
require condition (second's images' status = 0) reporting "Releasing one view changed another view's image"
close the address of view
close the address of second
close the address of instance
print line "Pictures cache per view, reflow on decode, fit without distortion and release pending resources."
